# PBE on LiH with Grimme's D3 empirical dispersion correction.
#
# The `dispersion` keyword adds a closed-form, geometry-only term to the total
# energy and to the nuclear gradient. It touches neither the density nor the
# Fock matrix, so the SCF converges to the same orbitals it would without it;
# what changes is the energy it reports and the forces it hands the optimizer.
#
#   dispersion             none | d3bj | d3zero
#   dispersion_functional  which parameter set to use; `none` derives it from
#                          the first token of `xc` (here: pbe)
#   dispersion_atm         three-body Axilrod-Teller-Muto term, off by default
#                          (and identically zero for a two-atom system)
#
# Requires MADNESS to be built against simple-dftd3 AND libxc; the case is not
# registered otherwise. libxc is needed for `xc pbe` alone -- and dropping to
# `xc lda` would not help, because simple-dftd3 carries no LDA damping
# parameters. `derivatives 1` is on so the gradient carries the correction too --
# this is the only deck here that asserts a single-point gradient component.
#
# Run:   ./run.sh          (or: madqc --wf=scf scf_lih_pbe_d3.in)

dft
    xc          pbe
    dispersion  d3bj
    protocol    [1e-4]
    dconv       1e-4
    derivatives 1
end

molecule
    units   atomic
    eprec   1e-6
    Li  0.0  0.0  0.0
    H   0.0  0.0  3.0
end
